#: ../../<rst_prolog>:50
msgid ""
"Use the More icon in the top left corner to access Mattermost desktop "
"apps customization settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-tasks.rst:58
msgid "An example of a playbook condition being added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-tasks.rst:61
msgid ""
"Select an attribute, condition, and value to define when the task should "
"be included. Then select **Done editing**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-tasks.rst:63
msgid "An example of a playbook condition with values defined."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-tasks.rst:66
msgid ""
"Conditional tasks are evaluated and automatically added to or removed "
"from the checklist based on defined conditions. This reduces cognitive "
"load by showing only relevant tasks and ensures that critical steps "
"aren't overlooked in different scenarios."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-tasks.rst:69
msgid "You can add up to 2 conditions per task to create an either/or condition."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-tasks.rst:72
msgid "Task inbox"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-tasks.rst:74
msgid ""
"In addition to the daily digest, you also have access to a task inbox. "
"The task inbox provides you with a cross-run overview of the tasks you're"
" accountable for, sorted by due date."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-tasks.rst:76
msgid "You can:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-tasks.rst:78
msgid "Access each task directly, without having to visit the individual runs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-tasks.rst:79
msgid "Mark tasks as complete or skip them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-tasks.rst:80
msgid ""
"Change the task assignee from yourself to another team member. The task "
"will then be removed from your inbox."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-tasks.rst:81
msgid "You can change the due date of tasks to manage priorities and urgency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/workflow-automation/work-with-tasks.rst:83
msgid ""
"To view your task inbox, access the **Playbooks** tab in Mattermost. In "
"the header, next to your profile image, select the tasks list icon. A "
"list of every task assigned to you from every run that's in progress is "
"displayed."
msgstr ""

